Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from a lack of configurability in the handling of failures when creating Write-Ahead Log (WAL) files in HDFS. Previously, the system would halt after a fixed number of WAL creation errors (5), which may not be suitable for all environments. The new configuration properties allow users to specify their own thresholds for failures, preventing premature termination of the TabletServer due to transient HDFS issues.

